# ModelSim
work/
transcript
vsim.wlf
modelsim.ini
sim/**/*.log

# Local build/debug scratch: Quartus run logs and hardware screenshots pulled
# back by scripts/mister_hw_test.py during bring-up. Regenerable, and the
# screenshots are only meaningful alongside the temporary debug build that
# produced them.
quartus_*.log
scratch_*.png

# Local MiSTer connection settings (host/user/password) for
# scripts/mister_hw_test.py -- never committed, see the file's own header.
mister.env

# ModelSim crash dumps.
*.vstf

# Decoded debug-tap captures and other local analysis scratch.
scratch_*.txt

# releases/ IS the right home for built bitstreams -- they just aren't
# tracked for now, while the core still doesn't run the games. Only a build
# VERIFIED to actually run belongs in git: committing one that merely
# compiles is actively misleading (one such build was committed and had to
# be removed -- it predated the timing-closure fix and did not run at all).
# When there is a verified build worth publishing, add it deliberately:
#   git add -f "releases/<name>.rbf"
releases/*.rbf

# vasm: NOT vendored (license is non-commercial/no-modification
# redistribution, see tools/README.md) -- built locally on demand by
# scripts/fetch_build_vasm.sh instead. Assembled test-program outputs are
# regenerable build artifacts, not source; the .s files are what's tracked.
tools/vasm/
sim/**/*.bin
sim/**/*.lst
sim/**/*.hex

# Copyrighted MAME ROM dumps used for local bring-up/verification -- never
# committed, regardless of subdirectory.
roms/

# Ad-hoc hardware capture scratch. Screenshots pulled off the MiSTer and their
# decoded traces pile up fast during bring-up; the ones worth keeping are named
# and committed under debug/ explicitly. scripts/decode_trace.py writes every
# decode to debug/captures/ keyed by capture type and settings, so those persist
# locally as a comparison record without entering the repo.
/*.png
/*.txt
debug/captures/
